WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.428
[sighs]

2
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.889
Phil and I process very differently.

3
00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:18.852
{\an8}and so I am kind of a hard-ass.
and I'm the complete opposite.

4
00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:23.523
{\an8}I have my guard up at all times.
don't tell anyone how I feel.

5
00:00:23.606 --> 00:00:25.900
and. uh. and I don't ask for help.

6
00:00:26.818 --> 00:00:30.363
{\an8}Phil is very much
a heart-on-his-sleeve kind of guy.

7
00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:34.409
{\an8}He seems like.
you know. he's scary and tough. but…

8
00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:38.705
{\an8}And he is. but on the inside.
he's very vulnerable.

9
00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.749
[producer] How'd it go? How you feeling?

10
00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.549
Uh…

11
00:00:49.632 --> 00:00:51.051
I feel good. [chuckles]

12
00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:53.636
[producer] What's on your mind. man?
Looks like something.

13
00:00:54.596 --> 00:00:55.638
Mm…

14
00:01:04.773 --> 00:01:06.941
I'm doing my best to not fall apart.

15
00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:08.151
but after…

16
00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.362
The night's over.
I can fall apart now. and…

17
00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:14.324
I got a…
I got a heavy heart right now. It's…

18
00:01:14.866 --> 00:01:16.493
[producer] Can I ask in what regard?

19
00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:18.578
Uh…

20
00:01:20.663 --> 00:01:22.707
You can ask. I don't gotta tell.

21
00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.336
I don't have the best poker face.

22
00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:32.175
uh. and I tried my best to. to hide it.
because we didn't tell the world yet.

23
00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:35.678
and I made a… we promised each other
we weren't gonna tell anybody.

24
00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.931
[sniffles] Um…

25
00:01:38.014 --> 00:01:39.432
[inhales shakily]

26
00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:41.351
[sighs]

27
00:01:44.312 --> 00:01:45.563
[taps hands]

28
00:01:46.397 --> 00:01:48.316
We waited to…

29
00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.151
[sniffles]

30
00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:52.695
…announce to the world that. uh…

31
00:01:56.324 --> 00:01:57.742
[sniffles. sighs]

32
00:01:57.826 --> 00:01:59.327
You know… [chuckles]

33
00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:02.038
…I like to say
Larry went back to his home planet.

34
00:02:02.831 --> 00:02:04.582
[solemn music playing]

35
00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:18.847
{\an8}[CM Punk] Larry was
a very special little dude.

36
00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:22.976
He. he came with a bite on his record.
so he was a little criminal.

37
00:02:23.059 --> 00:02:26.980
He was a perfect example
of… a little misfit

38
00:02:27.063 --> 00:02:29.774
that needed to find his people.

39
00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:33.486
No different than me.
No different than AJ. [sniffles]

40
00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:38.241
They warned us. they said. you know.
if he gets another bite on his record.

41
00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.285
you know. by law.
they have to put him down.

42
00:02:40.368 --> 00:02:44.122
That's why I was always
so protective of. uh. of Larry. [sniffles]

43
00:02:44.789 --> 00:02:47.167
We don't have kids.
We don't have a lot of family.

44
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:50.211
You know.
it was just us and Larry for a decade.

45
00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:53.173
Um. so it was like losing a family member.

46
00:02:54.215 --> 00:02:57.343
Larry was this emotional support for me.

47
00:02:58.303 --> 00:03:03.057
And the past few years
as he turned to a senior dog.

48
00:03:03.141 --> 00:03:06.227
I became his. like.
emotional support human… [chuckles]

49
00:03:06.311 --> 00:03:08.396
…and he never left my side.

50
00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:13.693
Larry got sick.
and it took him pretty fast.

51
00:03:15.612 --> 00:03:17.322
{\an8}[CM Punk] That <i>Survivor Series</i>.

52
00:03:17.822 --> 00:03:19.616
{\an8}the very last minute that day.

53
00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:23.953
{\an8}I just asked to get a patch
put on the jacket that said "Larry's Dad."

54
00:03:26.831 --> 00:03:29.000
It might not seem like a big deal. but.

55
00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.254
uh. you know. it's a big deal to me.
So I just…

56
00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:38.218
I love the little dude.
So I just wanted him to…

57
00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:39.636
[sniffles]

58
00:03:40.595 --> 00:03:43.139
…I just wanted him to be with me
that day. that's all.

59
00:03:49.854 --> 00:03:51.064
[music fades]

60
00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.983
[intriguing music playing]

61
00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.652
[crowd cheering]

62
00:03:58.446 --> 00:03:59.864
[music fades]

63
00:04:02.617 --> 00:04:05.995
{\an8}So we can try to do the best job possible

64
00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:09.165
{\an8}of laying out long-term story arcs.

65
00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.001
and then life happens.

66
00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.379
{\an8}Plans change.

67
00:04:14.462 --> 00:04:17.298
{\an8}Sometimes. it's for amazing reasons.

68
00:04:17.382 --> 00:04:21.886
Reasons that you are happy about.
talent are happy about.

69
00:04:22.387 --> 00:04:24.222
but they derail everything you have.

70
00:04:24.305 --> 00:04:29.769
{\an8}Like Naomi having to vacate
the WWE Women's Championship in August.

71
00:04:29.852 --> 00:04:32.939
You know what? All the women
back there in the locker room.

72
00:04:33.022 --> 00:04:35.316
y'all should be thanking one person.

73
00:04:36.484 --> 00:04:37.360
<i>One person.</i>

74
00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:38.903
[Jimmy chuckling]

75
00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.407
- [Naomi] Mm.
- [Jimmy and TJ laugh]

76
00:04:45.243 --> 00:04:47.578
<i>Yeah. They should be thanking Big Jim.</i>

77
00:04:47.662 --> 00:04:50.707
because without him. y'all know
y'all wouldn't have a chance

78
00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.375
to take this title off of me.

79
00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.335
But thanks to Big Jim…

80
00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:57.338
He like to Netflix and chill.
if you know what I mean.

81
00:04:57.422 --> 00:04:59.173
[TJ laughing]

82
00:04:59.924 --> 00:05:02.844
[crowd chanting] Baby Uso!
[clapping rhythmically] Baby Uso!

83
00:05:02.927 --> 00:05:04.762
I'm gonna leave my title here.

84
00:05:05.388 --> 00:05:08.182
and I'm gonna give you heifers
nine months and some change.

85
00:05:09.225 --> 00:05:14.188
And even if I gotta come back
breastfeeding with my baby in my arm.

86
00:05:14.897 --> 00:05:17.525
I'm coming back
to pick up where I left off.

87
00:05:17.608 --> 00:05:19.610
[crowd cheering]

88
00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.740
[crowd chanting] Baby Uso!
[clapping rhythmically]

89
00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:26.159
Baby Uso! [clapping rhythmically]

90
00:05:26.242 --> 00:05:28.911
Baby Uso! [clapping rhythmically]

91
00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:31.748
Baby Uso! [clapping rhythmically]

92
00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:34.917
Like everything in life.
when one door closes. another opens.

93
00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:39.130
Um. when Naomi has to
vacate her championship.

94
00:05:39.213 --> 00:05:41.007
it opens up an opportunity.

95
00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:44.677
And the opportunity
happens to be for a new talent.

96
00:05:45.303 --> 00:05:48.973
{\an8}[in Spanish] My real name is
Ana Stephanie Vaquer González.

97
00:05:49.057 --> 00:05:54.187
{\an8}My ring names have been Dark Angel
and Stephanie Vaquer.

98
00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:56.314
[rock music playing]

99
00:05:58.066 --> 00:06:00.360
[Cole in English] <i>"La Primera"</i>
<i>Stephanie Vaquer</i>

100
00:06:00.443 --> 00:06:02.487
<i>has taken WWE by storm.</i>

101
00:06:06.824 --> 00:06:10.203
[in Spanish] Maybe a lot of people say
my first language is Spanish.

102
00:06:10.286 --> 00:06:11.662
But I say no. it's wrestling.

103
00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:16.292
[Cole in English] Stephanie Vaquer has her
where she wants her.

104
00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:17.543
And here we go!

105
00:06:18.669 --> 00:06:19.754
Devil's Kiss!

106
00:06:20.338 --> 00:06:25.301
I've never seen a move activate
the WWE fans quite like the Devil's Kiss.

107
00:06:27.345 --> 00:06:30.264
[in Spanish] The people's reaction
was amazing.

108
00:06:30.348 --> 00:06:32.517
[Booker T in English] Are we gonna see it?

109
00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:33.768
Here we go.

110
00:06:33.851 --> 00:06:37.313
Huh! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah!

111
00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:39.315
Ah yeah!

112
00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:42.068
<i>♪ The torture began… ♪</i>

113
00:06:45.196 --> 00:06:47.031
It was kinda thrilling! [chuckles]

114
00:06:47.115 --> 00:06:49.117
[crowd chanting enthusiastically]

115
00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:54.747
The ass to the face might have been
the crowd's favorite moment.

116
00:06:56.457 --> 00:06:57.542
[music fades]

117
00:06:58.126 --> 00:07:00.253
[in Spanish] I was born
in San Fernando. Chile.

118
00:07:01.045 --> 00:07:03.923
My dad has always supported me
my whole life

119
00:07:04.006 --> 00:07:07.510
and was always there with me
watching WWE on TV.

120
00:07:08.553 --> 00:07:11.639
When I was 19. I moved to Mexico.

121
00:07:11.722 --> 00:07:16.686
which was the most accessible place
at the time to train for wrestling.

122
00:07:17.186 --> 00:07:21.357
I had no idea how dangerous
the path I was taking could be.

123
00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:23.526
[kids chanting in Spanish]

124
00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:26.696
[Vaquer] When I was starting my career.

125
00:07:27.447 --> 00:07:29.323
I had a facial fracture.

126
00:07:29.407 --> 00:07:31.075
[tense music playing]

127
00:07:31.659 --> 00:07:32.952
[dramatic music sting]

128
00:07:34.287 --> 00:07:37.123
My nose was in many little pieces.

129
00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:48.176
Three fractures in my nose

130
00:07:48.259 --> 00:07:50.428
and part of my cheekbone.

131
00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:56.893
It was very painful. I remember
I spent a month sleeping sitting up.

132
00:07:57.768 --> 00:08:02.231
And now I was in a country
where I didn't know anyone. I was alone.

133
00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:06.235
I couldn't train. I couldn't wrestle.
So I couldn't make money in any way.

134
00:08:07.904 --> 00:08:11.407
And I started working as a waitress
at a restaurant…

135
00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:14.660
[ceramic shattering]

136
00:08:14.744 --> 00:08:17.955
…waiting for it to heal
while I slept in the kitchen

137
00:08:18.039 --> 00:08:19.999
and worked during the day as a waitress.

138
00:08:21.209 --> 00:08:24.545
Many times. I thought about calling my dad
to tell him I was giving up.

139
00:08:25.087 --> 00:08:27.715
But he always had a word of support.

140
00:08:27.798 --> 00:08:29.717
He was always supporting me.

141
00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:31.344
Like my hero.

142
00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:34.514
[intriguing music playing]

143
00:08:34.597 --> 00:08:39.393
[Vaquer] I kept living in Mexico
but went to Japan for a few months.

144
00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:46.150
And I learned a great deal
of life philosophy. like kintsugi.

145
00:08:48.444 --> 00:08:50.738
The idea of kintsugi

146
00:08:52.031 --> 00:08:54.992
is sometimes pieces become stronger
than they were before.

147
00:09:02.458 --> 00:09:05.419
When a plate breaks.
they put it back together.

148
00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:11.050
A plate that's put back together
has more value

149
00:09:11.592 --> 00:09:15.388
because it was rebuilt.
and that has a different beauty.

150
00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:20.726
They put it together again
with gold or silver.

151
00:09:21.519 --> 00:09:23.104
It has a unique value.

152
00:09:24.355 --> 00:09:26.148
And that stuck with me deeply.

153
00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:29.610
That philosophy teaches that

154
00:09:30.945 --> 00:09:33.322
the scars shouldn't be hidden

155
00:09:33.406 --> 00:09:36.117
Because they are beautiful.
They make you stronger.

156
00:09:39.161 --> 00:09:43.791
And I wanted to expose it
by doing this makeup on my face

157
00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:47.461
exactly on the side
where I had fractured it.

158
00:09:49.213 --> 00:09:51.549
A lot of experiences.
not only in my personal life.

159
00:09:51.632 --> 00:09:52.675
but also in my career.

160
00:09:53.384 --> 00:09:54.927
made me break.

161
00:09:55.428 --> 00:09:58.848
But I'm stronger now. I'm a unique piece.

162
00:09:59.348 --> 00:10:01.017
I was reborn just like kintsugi.

163
00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.560
[music slowly fades]

164
00:10:10.568 --> 00:10:13.070
[Vaquer] My title match. <i>Wrestlepalooza</i>.

165
00:10:15.281 --> 00:10:19.910
The producers had an idea for the end
that was the Devil's Kiss.

166
00:10:19.994 --> 00:10:22.872
Then I said. "But no."

167
00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:25.791
"This is the most important match
of my life."

168
00:10:27.251 --> 00:10:29.962
I'm going to do the thing
that's hardest for me to pull off.

169
00:10:31.088 --> 00:10:34.675
{\an8}[in English] We decided on Stephanie's
finishing move to be used that day.

170
00:10:34.759 --> 00:10:36.135
Whether you hit it or not. or…

171
00:10:36.218 --> 00:10:38.346
AJ Styles used the Spiral Tap.

172
00:10:38.429 --> 00:10:41.557
This is. I would say.
Stephanie's variation of it.

173
00:10:41.641 --> 00:10:43.809
But it's unique to Stephanie.

174
00:10:44.894 --> 00:10:48.773
[Vaquer in Spanish] To be able to do
that move. I had to overcome many fears..

175
00:10:49.273 --> 00:10:51.525
Because every time
I was on top of the third rope.

176
00:10:51.609 --> 00:10:54.612
I kept telling myself. "I'll fall.
I'm going to break my neck."

177
00:10:54.695 --> 00:10:56.280
"I'll fracture something again."

178
00:10:56.364 --> 00:10:59.283
[Williams in English] Want her head there
or here? It doesn't matter? Okay.

179
00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:02.620
I've never seen
that move executed in that fashion.

180
00:11:02.703 --> 00:11:05.164
and it's very dangerous. very impressive.

181
00:11:05.247 --> 00:11:08.376
They're probably gonna want you to use.
when you go over from now on.

182
00:11:08.876 --> 00:11:10.002
the… the Spiral Tap.

183
00:11:10.086 --> 00:11:15.549
[in Spanish] I really want to achieve
my biggest dream with this move.

184
00:11:15.633 --> 00:11:17.051
[suspenseful music playing]

185
00:11:17.134 --> 00:11:21.430
{\an8}[Cole in English] <i>Stephanie Vaquer debuted</i>
<i>in WWE just over a year ago.</i>

186
00:11:21.514 --> 00:11:25.601
{\an8}<i>Tonight. an opportunity to win</i>
<i>the Women's World Championship.</i>

187
00:11:25.685 --> 00:11:28.688
<i>Her father is here tonight from Chile.</i>

188
00:11:31.065 --> 00:11:33.943
[Vaquer in Spanish] It was the first time
he had ever seen me wrestle live.

189
00:11:34.819 --> 00:11:37.405
But he was able to be present
in the moment

190
00:11:37.905 --> 00:11:40.449
when I fulfilled
the greatest dream of my career

191
00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:41.992
and the greatest of my life.

192
00:11:43.327 --> 00:11:45.121
[Barrett in English] Vaquer is
the real deal.

193
00:11:45.204 --> 00:11:48.624
and tonight could be
her biggest moment so far.

194
00:11:51.043 --> 00:11:53.254
[Vaquer in Spanish]
This isn't choreography.

195
00:11:53.337 --> 00:11:55.631
This is something
you feel. live. and create.

196
00:11:58.175 --> 00:12:01.178
To listen to the people.
feel the ring. feel the vibe.

197
00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.598
To feel the wrestling.

198
00:12:05.141 --> 00:12:06.517
to let it flow.

199
00:12:08.728 --> 00:12:12.523
[in English] All right. Devil's Kiss time.
Devil's Kiss. her old finish.

200
00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:17.278
[Barrett] Oh. here we go.
We're going bouncy-bouncy!

201
00:12:17.361 --> 00:12:19.321
[Cole] The Devil's Kiss!

202
00:12:19.405 --> 00:12:21.824
[crowd chanting enthusiastically]

203
00:12:24.076 --> 00:12:25.786
[suspenseful music playing]

204
00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:28.038
[crowd cheering]

205
00:12:29.582 --> 00:12:32.042
All right. Here comes the finish now.

206
00:12:32.126 --> 00:12:33.461
{\an8}[Cole] Stephanie.

207
00:12:34.211 --> 00:12:36.547
going up to the top rope!

208
00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:38.340
[crowd chanting] Stephanie!

209
00:12:38.424 --> 00:12:44.930
[in Spanish] I started practicing
that move many years ago.

210
00:12:45.014 --> 00:12:47.683
But before WWE. I never wanted to do it.

211
00:12:47.767 --> 00:12:49.643
[suspenseful music building]

212
00:12:51.312 --> 00:12:52.396
[crowd] Oh!

213
00:12:53.272 --> 00:12:54.940
[Vaquer] Because I always thought

214
00:12:55.024 --> 00:12:57.985
that the move had to happen
at a special moment.

215
00:12:58.486 --> 00:13:02.865
[Barrett in English] Stephanie Vaquer adds
a new wrinkle to her playbook!

216
00:13:02.948 --> 00:13:04.533
[McAfee] And hits it perfectly.

217
00:13:04.617 --> 00:13:07.286
[Cole] And she delivers
the version of a Spiral Tap!

218
00:13:07.369 --> 00:13:09.872
Stephanie Vaquer wins the championship!

219
00:13:09.955 --> 00:13:12.833
[Taylor] …World Champion.

220
00:13:12.917 --> 00:13:18.547
Stephanie Vaquer!

221
00:13:18.631 --> 00:13:20.424
[rock music playing]

222
00:13:21.759 --> 00:13:23.803
[pensive music playing]

223
00:13:26.639 --> 00:13:29.225
[in Spanish] When I was a little girl.
I told him.

224
00:13:29.725 --> 00:13:32.061
"One day. I'm going to be
champion of the WWE.

225
00:13:35.189 --> 00:13:37.650
And he saw me become champion.

226
00:13:42.238 --> 00:13:44.365
- I love you.
- [Hector] I love you too.

227
00:13:45.533 --> 00:13:47.076
[Vaquer] Happy birthday.

228
00:13:48.577 --> 00:13:50.246
[Cole in English] Tremendous family.

229
00:13:50.329 --> 00:13:53.040
Her dad and mom supported her
as a teenager

230
00:13:53.123 --> 00:13:56.001
to follow her dream.
which she has done tonight.

231
00:13:56.085 --> 00:13:59.421
[Barrett] Yeah. Héctor has a hand
in that championship.

232
00:14:02.967 --> 00:14:05.094
- Congratulations.
- [Vaquer] I don't want to cry anymore.

233
00:14:05.177 --> 00:14:07.304
Please. let it out. Let it out.

234
00:14:07.388 --> 00:14:08.806
[Vaquer sobbing]

235
00:14:09.557 --> 00:14:11.392
{\an8}[Hayes] Okay? You did great.

236
00:14:11.475 --> 00:14:13.769
{\an8}Man. you nailed that fucking finish.

237
00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:15.604
- It's emotions.
- [Vaquer] This?

238
00:14:15.688 --> 00:14:18.232
- Yeah.
- All my life. this is my dream.

239
00:14:18.315 --> 00:14:20.025
[Hayes] I'm so happy for you.

240
00:14:20.526 --> 00:14:22.736
Okay? But this is just the beginning.

241
00:14:23.821 --> 00:14:26.198
[in Spanish] The moment I won the belt…

242
00:14:26.282 --> 00:14:29.076
[sniffles] …it was the dream of my life.

243
00:14:29.577 --> 00:14:31.495
My dad was there… [sniffles]

244
00:14:32.079 --> 00:14:34.498
…always just. like… always supporting me.

245
00:14:35.165 --> 00:14:37.459
[delighted laughter]

246
00:14:38.168 --> 00:14:39.378
[sighs happily]

247
00:14:39.461 --> 00:14:42.506
- You're beautiful. I love you. [kisses]
- [Vaquer sobbing]

248
00:14:46.594 --> 00:14:48.637
I dreamed so much about this.

249
00:14:49.138 --> 00:14:51.849
[Hector] You did it. beautiful.

250
00:14:55.436 --> 00:14:56.979
[music fades]

251
00:15:03.527 --> 00:15:07.197
{\an8}[Hunter in English] All these situations
have positives and negatives.

252
00:15:07.698 --> 00:15:11.660
{\an8}Sometimes. it's an amazing opportunity
for somebody.

253
00:15:12.161 --> 00:15:14.496
uh. like in the case of Stephanie Vaquer.

254
00:15:15.247 --> 00:15:20.502
Other times. that opportunity goes away
for somebody like Bron Breakker.

255
00:15:20.586 --> 00:15:25.174
who has basically the world at his feet
in front of him.

256
00:15:26.258 --> 00:15:28.844
And then all of a sudden.
all comes off the table.

257
00:15:29.845 --> 00:15:31.221
[Cole] Live on <i>Monday Night Raw</i>.

258
00:15:31.305 --> 00:15:34.308
Bron Breakker has made his way
out to ringside tonight.

259
00:15:34.391 --> 00:15:37.436
And. uh. I don't like
the look on his face. Corey.

260
00:15:39.813 --> 00:15:43.442
{\an8}I was supposed to destroy the set.
Get as mad as I possibly could.

261
00:15:43.525 --> 00:15:45.152
[uneasy music playing]

262
00:15:46.111 --> 00:15:48.739
[Breakker] Had nothing to do
with physicality or anything like that.

263
00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.283
It happened when I was screaming.

264
00:15:51.367 --> 00:15:53.285
You wanna ruin my Royal Rumble?

265
00:15:53.369 --> 00:15:56.413
I'll ruin your entire show!
Screw <i>Monday Night Raw</i>!

266
00:15:56.497 --> 00:15:58.457
My entire midsection locked up.

267
00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:01.543
I went to the back.
We still had one more shot to do.

268
00:16:02.544 --> 00:16:04.505
I was in the locker room. and

269
00:16:05.255 --> 00:16:08.592
I was just kind of. like. hunched over.
kind of holding my stomach.

270
00:16:08.676 --> 00:16:10.344
like. "What the hell just happened?"

271
00:16:10.427 --> 00:16:12.680
And when I went to stand up
to do the second shot.

272
00:16:12.763 --> 00:16:15.557
I couldn't. couldn't stand up.
My stomach was…

273
00:16:16.433 --> 00:16:21.397
Like. I couldn't… couldn't come out
of. like. this hunched-over.

274
00:16:21.897 --> 00:16:24.441
feel-sorry-for-me crap. so…

275
00:16:25.567 --> 00:16:27.486
Ultimately. I went into medical.

276
00:16:28.612 --> 00:16:31.490
I said. "I think something's going on.
I think it's a hernia."

277
00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:34.284
{\an8}Breakker got a hernia.

278
00:16:34.785 --> 00:16:36.286
{\an8}- [Roode] Oh shit.
- Yeah.

279
00:16:36.787 --> 00:16:39.790
- Tonight?
- I don't know. He said it just popped up.

280
00:16:40.708 --> 00:16:42.251
Can't get it to go back in.

281
00:16:43.252 --> 00:16:45.170
The doc took one look at it. like. "Yeah."

282
00:16:45.254 --> 00:16:47.881
"We need to go to the hospital right now.
get surgery."

283
00:16:47.965 --> 00:16:49.049
So I was like…

284
00:16:54.013 --> 00:16:55.889
I just kinda let everybody down.

285
00:16:56.473 --> 00:16:57.766
[sighs]

286
00:16:58.851 --> 00:16:59.852
It sucked.

287
00:17:01.979 --> 00:17:05.774
'Cause I'd gone on this journey…
for a year.

288
00:17:05.858 --> 00:17:07.317
[sniffles]

289
00:17:07.401 --> 00:17:08.736
[music fades]

290
00:17:08.819 --> 00:17:11.321
Put all this work in. done all this stuff.

291
00:17:11.864 --> 00:17:14.283
[inhales deeply. sighs]

292
00:17:14.366 --> 00:17:15.909
My body quit on me.

293
00:17:16.618 --> 00:17:20.122
There's nothing I could do.
Otherwise. I would have done it.

294
00:17:21.206 --> 00:17:23.876
[Hunter] If they have to put him back
into surgery. how long?

295
00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:26.420
{\an8}- [Prichard] How long until he's back?
- Yeah.

296
00:17:27.296 --> 00:17:29.256
[Prichard] Same thing as Austin Theory.

297
00:17:29.339 --> 00:17:30.549
Several months.

298
00:17:32.301 --> 00:17:34.428
It's the same injury as Austin Theory.

299
00:17:36.055 --> 00:17:37.514
[Hunter chuckling] Fuck. man.

300
00:17:40.851 --> 00:17:45.064
{\an8}Our doctors and our medical…
still feel the same way.

301
00:17:45.147 --> 00:17:48.275
Six weeks of doing nothing. Healing.

302
00:17:48.776 --> 00:17:52.821
At which time.
you can start to… do some stuff.

303
00:17:52.905 --> 00:17:56.366
Not six weeks back in the ring.
It's six weeks before he can get in the…

304
00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:59.661
No. six weeks
before he can even start to train.

305
00:17:59.745 --> 00:18:02.539
Where are we now from <i>Mania</i>?
How many weeks?

306
00:18:02.623 --> 00:18:04.875
- [Prichard] Eleven. Ten now. right?
- [Ward] Ten.

307
00:18:05.876 --> 00:18:08.879
The feeling is. is if he were
to try to push to come back earlier.

308
00:18:08.962 --> 00:18:12.091
he runs the risk
of fucking it up even worse.

309
00:18:12.174 --> 00:18:14.468
[Hunter] The Vision is under attack
from real-life events

310
00:18:14.551 --> 00:18:16.678
on a day-to-day basis at this point.

311
00:18:17.971 --> 00:18:24.561
When Seth goes down. we pivot
to mostly Bron Breakker and Bronson Reed.

312
00:18:24.645 --> 00:18:25.938
We add in Logan Paul.

313
00:18:26.021 --> 00:18:31.026
{\an8}We add in Austin Theory
to form this four-man group.

314
00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:33.821
{\an8}But before that can really get rolling.

315
00:18:34.363 --> 00:18:37.282
{\an8}Bron Breakker goes down with an injury.

316
00:18:37.783 --> 00:18:41.120
{\an8}We now have to pivot to Bronson Reed.

317
00:18:42.496 --> 00:18:44.873
{\an8}[Koskey] It seems like
the next natural one would be Bronson.

318
00:18:44.957 --> 00:18:47.417
Bronson was part of the attack.
They have the history.

319
00:18:47.501 --> 00:18:49.711
if this is all playing out
like it is Seth.

320
00:18:49.795 --> 00:18:52.881
This is setting up in a story
with Bronson Reed out of this

321
00:18:52.965 --> 00:18:54.591
who kind of usurps it a little bit.

322
00:18:54.675 --> 00:18:56.593
And now maybe Bron. if he can.

323
00:18:56.677 --> 00:18:59.513
comes back and actually costs Seth
the match at <i>WrestleMania</i>.

324
00:18:59.596 --> 00:19:03.517
When I asked earlier. like.
"What is Bron's…? How many weeks?"

325
00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:05.477
I wasn't asking for <i>Mania</i>.

326
00:19:05.561 --> 00:19:08.522
I was asking.
"Can he do a run-in at <i>Mania.</i>

327
00:19:08.605 --> 00:19:11.692
fuck over Seth.
and could he go to <i>Backlash</i>?"

328
00:19:17.948 --> 00:19:21.326
Now that… [sighs]
…we have lost Bron Breakker.

329
00:19:22.202 --> 00:19:26.582
we decide to pivot and put the full weight
of The Vision behind Bronson Reed.

330
00:19:26.665 --> 00:19:28.500
[intriguing music playing]

331
00:19:28.584 --> 00:19:30.419
[Hunter] And let's see
what he can do with it.

332
00:19:33.088 --> 00:19:36.049
But this thing is falling apart.
It's snakebit.

333
00:19:41.555 --> 00:19:43.724
[Reed] Fucking… I tore my bicep.

334
00:19:47.561 --> 00:19:49.813
[crowd] Oh…

335
00:19:49.897 --> 00:19:51.231
[crowd cheering]

336
00:19:51.315 --> 00:19:52.941
One. two…

337
00:19:55.819 --> 00:19:57.196
[Reed] Hey. ref.

338
00:19:57.696 --> 00:19:59.156
I tore my bicep.

339
00:20:01.658 --> 00:20:03.452
Bronson tore his bicep.

340
00:20:03.535 --> 00:20:05.287
His tricep. His tricep. Tricep.

341
00:20:05.954 --> 00:20:07.581
[indistinct chattering]

342
00:20:07.664 --> 00:20:10.292
Bicep. Bicep. Yup. Yup.

343
00:20:10.375 --> 00:20:14.463
[Cole] And Reed. uh. rolled out
of the ring after that German suplex.

344
00:20:14.546 --> 00:20:16.423
I think it shook Reed up a bit.

345
00:20:17.382 --> 00:20:20.886
[woman] We continually were like.
"Why do they keep getting cursed?"

346
00:20:21.678 --> 00:20:24.014
It was just one after one after one.

347
00:20:24.097 --> 00:20:26.016
{\an8}But for them. it's devastating.

348
00:20:26.099 --> 00:20:30.062
{\an8}Like. you have a goal or something
that you think you're going to achieve.

349
00:20:30.145 --> 00:20:31.897
and it gets ripped out from under you.

350
00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:34.942
Then you have to go home and watch
someone else slide into that spot

351
00:20:35.025 --> 00:20:36.526
because the show never stops.

352
00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:38.195
It was awful.

353
00:20:38.695 --> 00:20:41.490
{\an8}Yeah. I… I felt it tear.
and I was like. "Fuck!"

354
00:20:41.573 --> 00:20:44.993
{\an8}And then I had to take the German.
and I was like. "Okay. that's fine."

355
00:20:45.077 --> 00:20:47.996
I took the German. and then I just rolled.
and I said to Spider.

356
00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:49.748
I'm like. "My bicep's fucking torn."

357
00:20:49.831 --> 00:20:51.625
- Damn.
- Yeah. fuck it. Yeah.

358
00:20:51.708 --> 00:20:52.834
Damn.

359
00:20:52.918 --> 00:20:55.212
- The group. man. Is it cursed?
- That's what I said.

360
00:20:55.295 --> 00:20:57.422
- Fuck.
- The Vision's cursed.

361
00:20:57.506 --> 00:20:58.882
Be careful.

362
00:20:58.966 --> 00:21:00.968
[Hunter] Injuries are beginning
to pile up.

363
00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:04.638
So as <i>Elimination Chamber</i>
now looms on the horizon.

364
00:21:04.721 --> 00:21:08.433
which is the last big stop
before we get to <i>WrestleMania.</i>

365
00:21:09.184 --> 00:21:12.312
{\an8}we have big plans for CM Punk and AJ Lee.

366
00:21:12.396 --> 00:21:14.940
{\an8}but they are still processing their loss.

367
00:21:16.191 --> 00:21:18.026
After Larry passed.

368
00:21:19.027 --> 00:21:22.322
the fans. without provocation.

369
00:21:22.406 --> 00:21:25.158
started donating so much money
to PAWS Chicago.

370
00:21:25.242 --> 00:21:27.286
which is where we adopted Larry.

371
00:21:27.369 --> 00:21:29.204
And so we donated.

372
00:21:29.288 --> 00:21:31.581
and then the company donated.

373
00:21:31.665 --> 00:21:34.376
and we wanted to go to PAWS
to deliver this check.

374
00:21:35.085 --> 00:21:37.504
I love. you know. animals so much.

375
00:21:37.587 --> 00:21:40.257
so I found it to be
a comforting experience.

376
00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:42.384
I don't think Phil did. I think Phil…

377
00:21:43.677 --> 00:21:46.179
It brought up a lot.
so he needed a moment.

378
00:21:46.263 --> 00:21:49.224
[AJ] It's either "I'll never get
a dog again." 'cause I am dead inside…

379
00:21:49.308 --> 00:21:50.517
This is not easy.

380
00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:53.186
- [AJ] There's nothing left. Larry took it.
- [woman] Yup.

381
00:21:53.687 --> 00:21:57.024
{\an8}I anonymously.
and now it's not so anonymous. obviously.

382
00:21:57.107 --> 00:22:01.111
{\an8}but I… I donated a lot of money then
because it's just a special place

383
00:22:01.194 --> 00:22:04.031
'cause that's where
we all found each other.

384
00:22:04.114 --> 00:22:05.741
and I think they do amazing work

385
00:22:05.824 --> 00:22:09.411
and I'm very much somebody
who thinks dogs. more often than not.

386
00:22:09.494 --> 00:22:11.330
are. are better than most people.

387
00:22:11.413 --> 00:22:14.082
So I think it's a good cause.

388
00:22:14.583 --> 00:22:17.169
Oh! Oh my gosh. I'm not gonna make it.

389
00:22:17.252 --> 00:22:19.671
Oh my goodness! [chuckles]

390
00:22:19.755 --> 00:22:21.256
I cannot walk two feet.

391
00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:22.674
Hi!

392
00:22:22.758 --> 00:22:24.384
[CM Punk] So where
do you wanna buy a farm?

393
00:22:24.468 --> 00:22:27.804
- I know. just pack them up.
- [CM Punk] What do you think?

394
00:22:27.888 --> 00:22:30.265
- Tennessee?
- [AJ] Yeah. you know.

395
00:22:30.891 --> 00:22:35.145
That's what I was saying. It's either
no dogs ever again or 40 dogs.

396
00:22:36.438 --> 00:22:37.647
There's no in between.

397
00:22:38.148 --> 00:22:40.817
The way you're behaving.
one of those is an option.

398
00:22:40.901 --> 00:22:42.402
[laughter]

399
00:22:42.486 --> 00:22:46.448
[AJ] I think being around any dog
for a while is gonna be really hard.

400
00:22:46.531 --> 00:22:49.618
but it also feels like healing
in some ways. too.

401
00:22:49.701 --> 00:22:53.622
just to. like. have that puppy energy
or old man puppy energy.

402
00:22:53.705 --> 00:22:54.831
That's my favorite.

403
00:22:54.915 --> 00:22:56.416
[CM Punk] She's a little girl.

404
00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:57.959
'Cause they're so special.

405
00:22:58.043 --> 00:23:01.963
With Larry. we got to experience
just how magical senior dogs are.

406
00:23:02.047 --> 00:23:04.758
and there's so many
that need love and care and homes.

407
00:23:04.841 --> 00:23:06.760
So when we're healed.

408
00:23:06.843 --> 00:23:11.515
maybe one day
we get 30 seniors. [chuckles]

409
00:23:23.902 --> 00:23:26.947
[CM Punk] I'm not a religious man.
I don't say this about many places.

410
00:23:27.531 --> 00:23:29.574
We are in church right now.

411
00:23:30.075 --> 00:23:31.743
This is a holy place.

412
00:23:31.827 --> 00:23:35.122
the home of. uh. the Chicago Blackhawks
and the Chicago Bulls.

413
00:23:35.622 --> 00:23:37.332
I'm nobody without this place.

414
00:23:37.416 --> 00:23:41.169
The CM stands for "Chicago Made."
I'm at my best when I'm here.

415
00:23:41.253 --> 00:23:45.382
They push me to go harder. to go farther
than I probably would on my own.

416
00:23:45.465 --> 00:23:46.550
They carried me through

417
00:23:46.633 --> 00:23:49.344
some of the greatest moments
I've had here in WWE.

418
00:23:49.428 --> 00:23:51.555
{\an8}I think tonight's gonna be
one of those moments.

419
00:23:52.389 --> 00:23:58.228
[Hunter] This is sort of the last big stop
for us on the way to <i>WrestleMania</i>.

420
00:23:58.728 --> 00:24:02.732
knowing where we were going to get here
to CM Punk in this venue.

421
00:24:03.358 --> 00:24:05.444
in his hometown. as champ.

422
00:24:05.527 --> 00:24:07.446
There's nothing else like it
on the planet.

423
00:24:08.572 --> 00:24:11.741
It's a huge night for me and my family.
It's a huge night for AJ.

424
00:24:11.825 --> 00:24:13.869
her first singles match in over ten years.

425
00:24:13.952 --> 00:24:18.123
She's taking on. uh. old crazy Becky
for the Intercontinental Championship.

426
00:24:18.206 --> 00:24:20.250
You know. those are…
those are high stakes.

427
00:24:22.794 --> 00:24:24.838
Is there a way to get smoke in this?

428
00:24:25.338 --> 00:24:26.423
Sure.

429
00:24:26.506 --> 00:24:30.469
{\an8}[Hunter] Can you pop the little hole here
and you stuck a small tube to fill this?

430
00:24:30.552 --> 00:24:32.721
{\an8}[Trick] Yeah. man.
tonight I got something special.

431
00:24:32.804 --> 00:24:34.723
{\an8}Triple H pulled me to the side and said.

432
00:24:34.806 --> 00:24:37.434
{\an8}"We wanna do something different
for the Elimination Chamber."

433
00:24:37.517 --> 00:24:39.060
"Now let me know what you think."

434
00:24:39.144 --> 00:24:42.939
One upgrade I'd like to do
is… pop a hole or something

435
00:24:43.023 --> 00:24:44.983
so we can fill this…

436
00:24:45.108 --> 00:24:48.737
we can fill this. uh. glass chamber
with some smoke

437
00:24:48.820 --> 00:24:51.531
and get some little holes here
so when you're on it.

438
00:24:51.615 --> 00:24:55.035
smoke is kind of billowing up around you.
You know what I mean?

439
00:24:55.118 --> 00:24:57.162
Even. even if it's filling up your coat.

440
00:24:57.245 --> 00:25:00.790
I think everybody's gonna go crazy
tonight. so we got one.

441
00:25:01.291 --> 00:25:03.043
["Whoop That Trick" playing]

442
00:25:20.602 --> 00:25:24.731
[Hunter] The only thing you gotta
be cautious of is looking like a star.

443
00:25:24.814 --> 00:25:27.776
getting off that motherfucking shit.
Not like "Oh shit!" You know?

444
00:25:27.859 --> 00:25:31.112
- [man] Trip Williams.
- [Hunter] Trip Williams. There you go.

445
00:25:31.696 --> 00:25:33.323
One positive happening here

446
00:25:33.406 --> 00:25:37.661
is Seth Rollins is right at the line
of ready to return.

447
00:25:37.744 --> 00:25:40.372
and Seth's return is a big surprise.

448
00:25:41.456 --> 00:25:43.792
So we have Seth hiding out.

449
00:25:46.086 --> 00:25:48.630
[Rollins] It's just something
I've been doing for so long.

450
00:25:48.713 --> 00:25:51.883
{\an8}and I get accustomed to that feeling
of hearing the music

451
00:25:51.967 --> 00:25:54.010
{\an8}and feeling that reaction and that energy

452
00:25:54.094 --> 00:25:56.721
and that relationship you build
with a live audience.

453
00:25:56.805 --> 00:25:58.848
And so when you don't have that
for so long.

454
00:25:58.932 --> 00:26:01.935
people have asked.
"Are you ready to go back?"

455
00:26:02.018 --> 00:26:05.355
"Are you excited to go back?"
There's a lot of things I miss about it.

456
00:26:05.438 --> 00:26:08.775
but that feeling
of being the man in the arena.

457
00:26:08.858 --> 00:26:13.280
being the one out there doing the thing.
that's the thing that I miss the most.

458
00:26:14.322 --> 00:26:16.408
I've never seen anything like The Vision

459
00:26:17.325 --> 00:26:19.578
and the injuries that have been dealt.

460
00:26:20.370 --> 00:26:23.290
but it is part of the game.
That's the nature of what we do.

461
00:26:24.457 --> 00:26:27.794
There's always an element of excitement
that ups that

462
00:26:27.877 --> 00:26:30.130
when you're making your return
off an injury.

463
00:26:30.213 --> 00:26:32.257
and there's kind of some hype. and…

464
00:26:32.340 --> 00:26:35.427
I mean. couple that
with <i>WrestleMania </i>season.

465
00:26:35.510 --> 00:26:38.638
it's. uh… it's a good feeling.

466
00:26:39.306 --> 00:26:41.266
There it is. It's not too bad.

467
00:26:41.349 --> 00:26:43.184
Not the worst. not the best.

468
00:26:43.685 --> 00:26:49.316
Seth's going to return as a masked man
with a big reveal.

469
00:26:49.399 --> 00:26:53.236
but in order to make this work
and make sense.

470
00:26:53.320 --> 00:26:57.073
we need a decoy masked man
that will come in first.

471
00:26:57.157 --> 00:27:00.285
allowing Seth to make
his big. grand entrance.

472
00:27:00.785 --> 00:27:02.120
Logan eliminates LA.

473
00:27:02.203 --> 00:27:06.458
As they're getting LA out.
that opens the fucking door.

474
00:27:07.375 --> 00:27:09.461
- Masked guy. they catch him.
- Faux masked guy.

475
00:27:09.544 --> 00:27:11.671
- Faux masked guy. they catch him.
- Okay.

476
00:27:11.755 --> 00:27:13.298
Masked guy comes in.

477
00:27:13.381 --> 00:27:15.925
There's down…
whatever they're gonna do. Bang.

478
00:27:16.009 --> 00:27:18.637
Seth comes here.
Seth reveals as he's going to back out.

479
00:27:18.720 --> 00:27:20.513
He sees security coming. "Oh shit."

480
00:27:20.597 --> 00:27:24.476
Drops down. They go. chase. out. out.

481
00:27:24.559 --> 00:27:27.896
Run through the people
and just go out that vom.

482
00:27:27.979 --> 00:27:30.190
- [suspenseful music playing]
- [chuckles]

483
00:27:32.400 --> 00:27:34.819
I'm getting too old
for this shit. [chuckles]

484
00:27:34.903 --> 00:27:36.488
My wrists hurt.

485
00:27:39.824 --> 00:27:42.869
Kind of scared. but kind of calm.
and I think me being kind of calm

486
00:27:42.952 --> 00:27:45.705
is making me a little bit more scared.
to be honest.

487
00:27:45.789 --> 00:27:48.833
I don't think people realize
how high that actually is.

488
00:27:48.917 --> 00:27:50.752
because. yeah. it looks all good and fine

489
00:27:50.835 --> 00:27:54.506
when you're down here looking up.
but when you're up there looking down.

490
00:27:54.589 --> 00:27:56.299
it's a completely different story.

491
00:27:56.383 --> 00:27:58.176
Like. it's high.

492
00:27:58.259 --> 00:27:59.511
I'm scared.

493
00:28:00.220 --> 00:28:04.432
It's really high.
and. like. I don't like heights that much.

494
00:28:04.933 --> 00:28:06.976
I like to do stupid shit.

495
00:28:07.060 --> 00:28:09.854
but I don't like
the fact that I have to look down.

496
00:28:09.938 --> 00:28:13.024
So hopefully adrenaline. uh. will kick in

497
00:28:13.108 --> 00:28:15.485
and. uh. make everything
a little bit more smoother.

498
00:28:17.737 --> 00:28:19.614
- [man] Push.
- [man 2] Oh my God!

499
00:28:19.698 --> 00:28:21.074
[Ripley] Yes!

500
00:28:21.157 --> 00:28:22.283
[screams playfully]

501
00:28:22.367 --> 00:28:23.785
I'm supposed to get…

502
00:28:23.868 --> 00:28:26.037
[tense music playing]

503
00:28:26.121 --> 00:28:27.330
[crowd cheering]

504
00:28:30.250 --> 00:28:34.087
{\an8}[Cole] <i>It is a menacing steel structure</i>

505
00:28:34.170 --> 00:28:36.548
{\an8}<i>known as the Elimination Chamber.</i>

506
00:28:39.050 --> 00:28:41.511
<i>Two miles of chain link.</i>

507
00:28:42.011 --> 00:28:43.930
<i>It will surround the ring.</i>

508
00:28:44.431 --> 00:28:46.307
<i>This is an elimination match.</i>

509
00:28:47.142 --> 00:28:50.103
<i>At regularly scheduled intervals.</i>
<i>a pod will open.</i>

510
00:28:50.603 --> 00:28:55.108
<i>Once you lose. either pinned or submitted.</i>
<i>you gotta head back to the locker room.</i>

511
00:28:55.191 --> 00:28:59.988
<i>The last woman standing</i>
<i>goes to </i>Wrestlemania<i>.</i>

512
00:29:00.071 --> 00:29:01.406
[bell dinging]

513
00:29:04.659 --> 00:29:05.744
[Cole] Oh!

514
00:29:05.827 --> 00:29:10.540
And Kiana rolled out of harm's way.
and Tiffany headfirst into the pod.

515
00:29:10.623 --> 00:29:11.958
[Barrett] Welcome to the Chamber.

516
00:29:12.041 --> 00:29:13.585
[Prichard] We can start that count.

517
00:29:13.668 --> 00:29:15.587
[crowd counting] Six. five.

518
00:29:15.670 --> 00:29:19.299
four. three. two. one…

519
00:29:19.883 --> 00:29:21.092
[buzzer sounds]

520
00:29:21.176 --> 00:29:23.136
[Cole] Rhea Ripley!

521
00:29:23.219 --> 00:29:24.179
Oh!

522
00:29:24.262 --> 00:29:25.764
Stay with Rhea.

523
00:29:25.847 --> 00:29:28.641
[Cole] Stratton now runs into a headbutt
by Ripley.

524
00:29:28.725 --> 00:29:34.355
[Barrett] Rhea "Bloody" Ripley is starting
to steamroller towards <i>Wrestlemania</i>.

525
00:29:34.439 --> 00:29:35.523
[chuckling] Ooh!

526
00:29:35.607 --> 00:29:36.816
That was awesome.

527
00:29:36.900 --> 00:29:39.027
Now stay with Kiana and Bliss.

528
00:29:39.110 --> 00:29:41.237
[Cole] No eliminations thus far.

529
00:29:41.321 --> 00:29:42.614
Kiana James caught.

530
00:29:46.326 --> 00:29:49.037
And a mist! A mist by Asuka to Bliss!

531
00:29:50.163 --> 00:29:51.664
Kiana rolls her up!

532
00:29:51.748 --> 00:29:53.958
Kiana eliminates Bliss!

533
00:29:55.794 --> 00:29:59.756
[announcer] Alexa Bliss
has been eliminated.

534
00:30:03.718 --> 00:30:05.178
[man] <i>This door is stuck.</i>

535
00:30:08.014 --> 00:30:10.517
DA. just talk to me now.
Only on this channel.

536
00:30:10.600 --> 00:30:12.060
What's wrong with the door?

537
00:30:13.269 --> 00:30:14.771
[DA] The pin's broken on it.

538
00:30:15.438 --> 00:30:17.857
[Prichard] Door's broken. The main door.

539
00:30:17.941 --> 00:30:19.526
It's stuck closed.

540
00:30:20.235 --> 00:30:21.820
Stuck closed right now.

541
00:30:22.779 --> 00:30:24.197
They're working on it.

542
00:30:25.198 --> 00:30:26.950
[Barrett] This is the danger zone
right now.

543
00:30:27.033 --> 00:30:29.744
as soon as you leave
the inside of those ropes.

544
00:30:29.828 --> 00:30:33.873
[Cole] And now a running powerslam
through the pod!

545
00:30:33.957 --> 00:30:35.375
Catching Asuka.

546
00:30:36.209 --> 00:30:39.254
In her arms. Tejana Bomb modified!

547
00:30:39.337 --> 00:30:41.381
Stacking up both women.

548
00:30:41.464 --> 00:30:44.634
Raquel eliminates James and Asuka.

549
00:30:45.134 --> 00:30:46.761
Is that door open or not?

550
00:30:46.845 --> 00:30:48.596
[DA] <i>Not yet. Not yet.</i>

551
00:30:48.680 --> 00:30:49.931
Roll them to the apron.

552
00:30:50.473 --> 00:30:51.683
[DA] Copy. told him.

553
00:30:55.019 --> 00:30:57.188
We gotta get that motherfucker open.

554
00:30:57.272 --> 00:30:58.523
Give me that crowbar.

555
00:30:58.606 --> 00:30:59.524
Yeah.

556
00:31:01.276 --> 00:31:03.194
[Hunter] We've just gotta get
that door open.

557
00:31:05.780 --> 00:31:07.615
Get everybody working on that.

558
00:31:12.495 --> 00:31:15.290
- It's fixed.
- [Prichard] We are clear. We're clear.

559
00:31:15.832 --> 00:31:17.834
[Cole] We are now down to three.

560
00:31:18.501 --> 00:31:20.920
Will it be Tiffany Stratton?
Will it be Rhea Ripley?

561
00:31:21.004 --> 00:31:22.672
Will it be Raquel Rodriguez?

562
00:31:22.755 --> 00:31:25.341
High stakes. high pressure here tonight.

563
00:31:25.425 --> 00:31:29.095
We're coming up on that spot
where Rhea comes off of the pod.

564
00:31:29.178 --> 00:31:30.638
Stay with Raquel.

565
00:31:30.722 --> 00:31:32.473
She's gonna set Rhea up.

566
00:31:32.557 --> 00:31:36.561
[Barrett] The powerhouse Raquel.
What the hell is she cooking up here?

567
00:31:36.644 --> 00:31:37.645
[Cole] Rhea caught.

568
00:31:37.729 --> 00:31:42.233
Raquel now trapping Rhea Ripley
in the steel chain link.

569
00:31:43.192 --> 00:31:44.986
[Jordan] Now you can start losing Rhea.

570
00:31:45.069 --> 00:31:48.615
Lose Rhea as much as you can.
Rhea's gonna start climbing that pod.

571
00:31:49.490 --> 00:31:53.453
This is to set Tiffany up. and then Rhea's
gonna come off the pod onto Raquel.

572
00:31:53.536 --> 00:31:56.372
[Cole] Raquel Rodriguez mauling Stratton.

573
00:31:56.873 --> 00:31:59.292
Meanwhile. Ripley on top of the pod!

574
00:32:00.418 --> 00:32:03.504
Cannonball to take out Raquel!

575
00:32:11.262 --> 00:32:14.891
[crowd chanting] Holy shit!
Holy shit! Holy shit!

576
00:32:14.974 --> 00:32:16.392
Tiffany. Tiffany. Tiffany.

577
00:32:16.476 --> 00:32:19.312
[Barrett] Wait up. Cole.
Oh. look who's on the top rope!

578
00:32:19.812 --> 00:32:23.942
[Cole] Stratton! Prettiest Moonsault Ever!

579
00:32:24.442 --> 00:32:26.069
Raquel is eliminated.

580
00:32:26.152 --> 00:32:27.737
We are down to two.

581
00:32:28.237 --> 00:32:30.698
[suspenseful music playing]

582
00:32:32.700 --> 00:32:35.161
[Cole] Tiffany Stratton gonna head up
to the top rope.

583
00:32:35.662 --> 00:32:39.540
Oh. went for the swanton.
Rhea Ripley rolled out of harm's way.

584
00:32:39.624 --> 00:32:44.337
Catches Tiffany now with a kick.
It could be Ripley's opportunity.

585
00:32:44.420 --> 00:32:47.507
- [Barrett] Just pure power from Ripley.
- [Cole] Look at this.

586
00:32:47.590 --> 00:32:49.676
- Boom!
- [Barrett] Ooh. jeez!

587
00:32:49.759 --> 00:32:52.428
[Cole] Stratton face-first.
Cover now by Rhea.

588
00:32:52.512 --> 00:32:53.846
And a kick-out.

589
00:32:54.847 --> 00:32:56.099
[Prichard] Tiffany okay?

590
00:32:57.684 --> 00:32:59.143
Bloody nose. she's fine.

591
00:32:59.644 --> 00:33:02.647
Okay. seeing the blood.
Don't worry about it.

592
00:33:03.147 --> 00:33:06.234
[Barrett] The wounds obvious
on the face of Tiffany Stratton now.

593
00:33:07.276 --> 00:33:08.861
[Cole] Tiffany Stratton up top.

594
00:33:08.945 --> 00:33:12.865
Looking for the Prettiest Moonsault Ever.
But driven into the pod by Ripley.

595
00:33:13.616 --> 00:33:14.951
Ripley…

596
00:33:15.034 --> 00:33:17.370
Riptide! Cover.

597
00:33:17.453 --> 00:33:18.871
[crowd counting] Two! Three!

598
00:33:18.955 --> 00:33:21.666
[Cole] Rhea's going to <i>WrestleMania</i>.

599
00:33:21.749 --> 00:33:23.501
[triumphant music playing]

600
00:33:27.714 --> 00:33:32.719
[Cole] What an incredible performance
by all six women tonight.

601
00:33:33.344 --> 00:33:35.888
[Hunter] You okay?
That was amazing. You break it?

602
00:33:35.972 --> 00:33:38.099
[Stratton] I don't know.
I'm kinda worried.

603
00:33:38.182 --> 00:33:40.727
- [Hunter] It doesn't look fucked up. Yeah.
- [Stratton] Okay.

604
00:33:41.853 --> 00:33:44.897
Not that it's great.
but it's worth a broken nose if you did.

605
00:33:44.981 --> 00:33:46.941
- It was great. Amazing job.
- Thank you.

606
00:33:47.025 --> 00:33:48.443
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

607
00:33:48.943 --> 00:33:50.945
Let's get Doc to look at it to make sure.

608
00:33:51.446 --> 00:33:53.740
It looks beautiful and straight. still.

609
00:33:53.823 --> 00:33:56.200
[TJ] Yeah. yeah. yeah. It is straight.

610
00:33:56.284 --> 00:33:58.453
- Yeah.
- My lips feel fucking numb.

611
00:33:58.536 --> 00:34:01.330
- [TJ] I think you probably ate it on the…
- Yeah.

612
00:34:01.414 --> 00:34:03.249
It came down so fast.

613
00:34:04.709 --> 00:34:06.294
[TJ] How'd the cannonball feel?

614
00:34:06.377 --> 00:34:08.921
It felt great. Better than the rehearsal.

615
00:34:09.547 --> 00:34:12.550
- Yeah. it's because you had adrenaline.
- I was like. "We're going!"

616
00:34:13.051 --> 00:34:15.470
[Hayes] Awesome. I mean awesome.

617
00:34:15.553 --> 00:34:17.889
Every one of you nailed it.

618
00:34:18.973 --> 00:34:20.516
Now we gotta go try to top it.

619
00:34:20.600 --> 00:34:22.727
- [Ripley] I know.
- That's what I wanted though.

620
00:34:22.810 --> 00:34:28.775
So Rhea fricking Ripley got me up
in the fricking electric chair.

621
00:34:28.858 --> 00:34:30.985
and I did not anticipate
the bump being so hard.

622
00:34:31.069 --> 00:34:33.821
and I did not catch myself.

623
00:34:34.489 --> 00:34:36.115
[crowd] Oh!

624
00:34:36.199 --> 00:34:37.867
[Stratton] I just face-planted.

625
00:34:39.285 --> 00:34:42.705
Basically. almost broke my nose
and chipped my tooth again.

626
00:34:42.789 --> 00:34:45.083
Isn't that lovely?
A little <i>WrestleMania </i>throwback.

627
00:34:45.166 --> 00:34:47.502
- Toodles!
- Toodles!

628
00:34:48.628 --> 00:34:52.673
When it happened. I was gushing blood.
but it's not broken.

629
00:34:52.757 --> 00:34:53.758
Doc pressed on it.

630
00:34:53.841 --> 00:34:56.761
He said he pressed on it pretty hard.
so we're in the clear.

631
00:34:56.844 --> 00:34:58.888
Thank God! I like my nose.

632
00:34:59.388 --> 00:35:02.433
I'm totally fine. Totally fine.

633
00:35:02.517 --> 00:35:06.562
No. it's not your fault. I just…
I did not anticipate coming down so fast.

634
00:35:07.355 --> 00:35:08.648
I know. It's okay.

635
00:35:08.731 --> 00:35:10.942
I'm gonna put my grills in
and take a cool pic.

636
00:35:11.025 --> 00:35:12.318
[TJ laughs]

637
00:35:13.653 --> 00:35:15.780
Can you show the blood
on your fingers as well?

638
00:35:15.863 --> 00:35:16.697
[Stratton] Yeah.

639
00:35:17.198 --> 00:35:19.158
[camera shutter clicking]

640
00:35:21.869 --> 00:35:23.287
One word.

641
00:35:25.832 --> 00:35:27.041
Four letters.

642
00:35:27.625 --> 00:35:28.626
Ouch.

643
00:35:29.502 --> 00:35:31.546
[intriguing music playing]

644
00:35:31.629 --> 00:35:33.756
- [Williams] Is April doing okay?
- [CM Punk] Yeah. Why?

645
00:35:33.840 --> 00:35:36.175
{\an8}[Williams] Just trying to engage her.

646
00:35:36.259 --> 00:35:38.302
{\an8}- I know she's nervous.
- She's stressed. Just nerves.

647
00:35:38.386 --> 00:35:40.054
{\an8}I wanna make sure she's comfortable.

648
00:35:40.138 --> 00:35:41.681
{\an8}- It's just butterflies.
- [Williams] Okay.

649
00:35:41.764 --> 00:35:45.351
- [CM Punk] I haven't heard anything bad.
- [Williams] Great. Okay.

650
00:35:45.434 --> 00:35:47.937
Puts a lot of pressure on herself.
like we do.

651
00:35:48.020 --> 00:35:50.857
First singles match in over ten years.
just so you know…

652
00:35:51.524 --> 00:35:54.318
- [Williams] Yep.
- I know how she feels. [chuckles]

653
00:35:55.403 --> 00:35:58.489
[Hunter] You haven't forgotten how.
You went away for a little bit.

654
00:35:58.573 --> 00:36:00.408
- Go out there and tear it up.
- Thank you.

655
00:36:01.576 --> 00:36:04.412
We had 20-something minutes
at our disposal.

656
00:36:04.495 --> 00:36:07.748
which… I don't know if you added up
all of my title matches.

657
00:36:07.832 --> 00:36:10.668
if they even equaled
22 minutes. [chuckling]

658
00:36:11.169 --> 00:36:14.672
So I was scared
I actually wouldn't be able to do it.

659
00:36:14.755 --> 00:36:17.258
Have fun. AJ. You got this.

660
00:36:18.718 --> 00:36:21.888
Just breathe. and you'll be fine.

661
00:36:22.430 --> 00:36:23.848
[uneasy music playing]

662
00:36:23.931 --> 00:36:30.730
{\an8}[announcer] The following contest is for
the Women's Intercontinental Championship.

663
00:36:30.813 --> 00:36:33.608
[crowd chanting] AJ Lee! AJ Lee!

664
00:36:33.691 --> 00:36:35.234
AJ Lee!

665
00:36:35.318 --> 00:36:37.486
[upbeat synth music playing]

666
00:36:37.570 --> 00:36:38.905
<i>♪ Let's light it up ♪</i>

667
00:36:38.988 --> 00:36:41.157
<i>♪ Light it up. light it up</i>
<i>Light it up tonight… ♪</i>

668
00:36:42.033 --> 00:36:46.120
[Cole] The woman
who now calls Chicago home. AJ Lee.

669
00:36:46.204 --> 00:36:48.873
will have the backing
of the majority of this crowd.

670
00:36:48.956 --> 00:36:52.460
<i>♪ Like the night. like the diamonds</i>
<i>As they shine in your eyes ♪</i>

671
00:36:54.003 --> 00:36:58.883
Just as an athlete. I was pretty scared
of what I was gonna be capable of.

672
00:36:58.966 --> 00:37:03.179
And mostly I was just. like. worrying
I was gonna need my inhaler out there.

673
00:37:03.262 --> 00:37:04.513
[uneasy music playing]

674
00:37:04.597 --> 00:37:07.725
[Barrett] The nerves in AJ Lee
are gonna be through the roof

675
00:37:07.808 --> 00:37:09.560
in this position.

676
00:37:11.938 --> 00:37:15.149
[Cole] Here comes Lee.
AJ Lee unloading on Becky Lynch.

677
00:37:18.861 --> 00:37:20.071
[Lynch grunts]

678
00:37:20.154 --> 00:37:22.698
[Cole] Becky just took out Jessika Carr!

679
00:37:22.782 --> 00:37:26.577
- [Barrett] Inadvertent. Don't spin that.
- [Cole] She didn't seem to give a damn.

680
00:37:26.661 --> 00:37:28.621
And now AJ Lee with a Black Widow.

681
00:37:28.704 --> 00:37:31.791
Becky's other side. Other side.
so she can tap with her hand.

682
00:37:32.375 --> 00:37:34.752
- There we go. There we go.
- [Cole] Becky's tapping!

683
00:37:34.835 --> 00:37:36.629
[Barrett] The ref doesn't see it!

684
00:37:36.712 --> 00:37:40.174
[Cole] Well. AJ Lee should be
the Intercontinental Champion right now.

685
00:37:41.509 --> 00:37:42.468
{\an8}AJ…

686
00:37:44.053 --> 00:37:46.639
Connecting knee-first with a steel chair.

687
00:37:46.722 --> 00:37:49.976
- [Barrett] That was an ugly landing.
- [Cole] Oh. and now the DDT.

688
00:37:50.059 --> 00:37:51.686
AJ may be out.

689
00:37:52.311 --> 00:37:54.438
Manhandle Slam!

690
00:37:54.522 --> 00:37:55.564
The cover.

691
00:37:55.648 --> 00:37:57.024
[crowd] One. two…

692
00:37:57.108 --> 00:37:58.985
[Cole] AJ kicked out!

693
00:37:59.068 --> 00:38:00.319
[crowd cheering]

694
00:38:01.279 --> 00:38:03.406
[Cole] And Becky can't believe it!

695
00:38:04.198 --> 00:38:07.118
[Barrett] Well. it might be
starting to dawn on the champ

696
00:38:07.201 --> 00:38:10.830
that tonight is just not your night.
Becky Lynch.

697
00:38:10.913 --> 00:38:14.583
[AJ] She wants to be
the best bad guy in the world.

698
00:38:14.667 --> 00:38:18.587
And she knows you need
a really good babyface

699
00:38:18.671 --> 00:38:19.672
to make that happen.

700
00:38:19.755 --> 00:38:24.010
- [crowd chanting] AJ Lee! AJ Lee!!
- [AJ] She makes you look like a star.

701
00:38:24.093 --> 00:38:26.429
And I feel like we nailed it.

702
00:38:26.512 --> 00:38:28.180
[suspenseful music playing]

703
00:38:29.307 --> 00:38:31.934
[Cole] Nice takedown by AJ Lee.
